1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,648
Now feature selection.

2
00:00:01,648 --> 00:00:02,847
Prepare X and y:

3
00:00:02,847 --> 00:00:12,435
one-hot encode the six categorical columns, giving a matrix of twelve thousand three hundred thirty rows by eighty five columns.

4
00:00:12,435 --> 00:00:17,529
Split with stratification, and fit the scaler on training rows only.

5
00:00:17,529 --> 00:00:20,376
All selection uses training rows only.

6
00:00:21,176 --> 00:00:21,935
Filter one:

7
00:00:21,935 --> 00:00:23,661
variance and correlation.

8
00:00:23,661 --> 00:00:36,705
A variance threshold of zero point oh one flags twenty three near-constant columns, though rates look constant only because of their scale, so apply this to zero-one dummies, not raw rates.

9
00:00:36,705 --> 00:00:41,882
For correlation, take the upper triangle and list the most redundant pairs:

10
00:00:41,882 --> 00:00:48,508
product related and total pages at zero point nine nine seven, and others above zero point nine.

11
00:00:48,508 --> 00:00:52,856
Pairs above point nine say the same thing, so keep one of each.

12
00:00:53,656 --> 00:00:54,492
Filter two:

13
00:00:54,492 --> 00:00:59,967
the A N O V A F-test and mutual information, both through Select K Best.

14
00:00:59,967 --> 00:01:09,318
Both rank log page values, has page value and page values at the top, followed by the two interaction terms and exit rates.

15
00:01:09,318 --> 00:01:13,120
Two different statistics agree on the same signal.

16
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,066
Wrapper methods:

17
00:01:15,066 --> 00:01:22,589
recursive feature elimination, about seventeen seconds, and forward selection, about twenty five seconds.

18
00:01:22,589 --> 00:01:29,538
R F E picks page values, has page value, bounce and exit rates, and month November, among others.

19
00:01:29,538 --> 00:01:36,846
Forward selection picks a different set, including total pages, product share and month March and May.

20
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:42,792
The wrappers take much longer than filters because they train the model many times.

21
00:01:43,592 --> 00:01:44,852
Embedded methods:

22
00:01:44,852 --> 00:01:51,521
an L one penalty with C of point oh two keeps twenty of eighty five coefficients non-zero.

23
00:01:51,521 --> 00:02:02,414
A random forest gives feature importances, with log page values at zero point one three two and page values at zero point one one seven at the top.

24
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:03,896
We keep the top ten.

25
00:02:04,696 --> 00:02:07,540
Compare every subset with the same model.

26
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:22,384
We collect all seven feature lists in a dictionary, define an evaluate function that fits logistic regression on train and scores test R O C A U C and F one, and apply it to each list with one call, no loop needed.

27
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:23,944
The result:

28
00:02:23,944 --> 00:02:28,231
ten well-chosen features are about as good as all eighty five.

29
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:37,218
Forward selection with ten features scores zero point nine one nine, higher than all eighty five features at point nine one eight.

30
00:02:37,218 --> 00:02:42,680
L one with twenty features gets point nine one five, R F E point nine oh seven.

31
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:51,944
The filters and random forest top ten drop to about point eight six five, because their lists repeat the page-value signal five times.

32
00:02:51,944 --> 00:02:55,608
Month November is chosen only by model-based methods.

33
00:02:56,408 --> 00:02:59,385
Which features do the methods agree on?

34
00:02:59,385 --> 00:03:02,743
A cross-tab counts votes out of six methods.

35
00:03:02,743 --> 00:03:08,468
Log page values, page value times Q four and page values get all six votes.

36
00:03:08,468 --> 00:03:13,582
Exit rates, has page value and page value times returning get five.

37
00:03:13,582 --> 00:03:19,993
The page-value family is picked by every method, the strongest evidence in the data.

38
00:03:19,993 --> 00:03:24,344
Features with one or two votes depend on the method used.

39
00:03:25,144 --> 00:03:28,284
The same steps on the Pima diabetes data.

40
00:03:28,284 --> 00:03:38,929
Zeros in glucose, blood pressure, skin thickness, insulin and BMI mean not measured, so replace them with missing and fill with the median.

41
00:03:38,929 --> 00:03:45,285
Construct flags for high glucose and obesity, a ratio, a log, and two interactions.

42
00:03:45,285 --> 00:03:51,412
The flags split the diabetes rate from twelve percent up to seventy six percent.

43
00:03:51,412 --> 00:03:53,556
But test A U C did not rise:

44
00:03:53,556 --> 00:03:59,606
zero point eight two three nine baseline versus zero point eight two three two.

45
00:03:59,606 --> 00:04:03,129
Glucose, BMI and age already carry the signal.

46
00:04:03,129 --> 00:04:04,048
Always test.

47
00:04:04,848 --> 00:04:09,375
On Pima, five selected features are about as good as all fourteen.

48
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:16,372
Forward selection with five features scores point eight two two against point eight two three for all.

49
00:04:16,372 --> 00:04:23,232
Glucose is chosen by every method, and five features stay within point oh two A U C of all fourteen.

50
00:04:24,032 --> 00:04:25,437
What the lab showed.

51
00:04:25,437 --> 00:04:34,079
Constructed features and interactions took test A U C from point eight five five to point nine oh four with the same model.

52
00:04:34,079 --> 00:04:41,738
Degree three polynomials on four hundred rows gave train point nine nine six and test point seven four three:

53
00:04:41,738 --> 00:04:43,143
the curse in action.

54
00:04:43,143 --> 00:04:48,905
Forward selection found that ten of eighty five columns give the full-model A U C.

55
00:04:48,905 --> 00:04:52,699
And the same pattern worked on the Pima diabetes data.

56
00:04:52,699 --> 00:04:54,104
Thanks for watching.

